WEBVTT

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:26.440
- Paul doesn't know anything about a computer. - Carnot, stop him.

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:17.580
- My mission.

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:19.240
- Security to mission.

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:36.280
Me?

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:22.790
check out our systems. It's his main mission. All sections report. All sections report.

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:24.770
Switch on the big screen. See if we can pick up anything.

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:56.180
You're losing picture, but you're gone.

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:02.670
The scanner shows that the object is not moving.

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:04.320
I do not understand.

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:05.560
Look at that monitor.

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:07.610
It is still getting closer to us.

00:04:07.610 --> 00:04:23.830
Sandra, are you sure that we're locked on its orbit?

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:25.350
Commander, the transmission coming in.

00:06:08.890 --> 00:06:13.220
- Commander, power failures in sectors G6, 8 and 11.

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:16.400
All transportation out.

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:17.420
- What about the main power unit?

00:06:17.420 --> 00:06:18.860
- I haven't been able to get through to Anderson.

00:06:18.860 --> 00:06:20.260
- Commander, I have his report.

00:06:20.260 --> 00:06:22.360
All nuclear generators and reactors check out,

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:24.540
but power is operating at only minimum capacity.

00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:26.950
- Sir, report from reconnaissance.

00:06:26.950 --> 00:06:28.840
All but four of our eagles are damaged.

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:39.320
defenceless. Cono, computer unable to make any calculations, insufficient data. Try every

00:06:39.320 --> 00:06:51.450
possible variable. Yes, sir. Why did they not destroy us? Paul, try to make contact with

00:06:51.450 --> 00:06:57.540
them. You sound, light, radio wave patterns, the entire frequency scale. Now tell Professor

00:06:57.540 --> 00:07:00.000
Bergman to come to my office, doctor. Helena, I want to know.

00:07:00.030 --> 00:07:02.150
Autopsy on Ted Clifford. I want to know exactly what killed him.

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:03.580
That might not be possible.

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:06.090
Make it possible. I want to know what we're up against.

00:07:09.040 --> 00:07:10.200
What do you know about the planet Triton?

00:07:10.440 --> 00:07:10.760
Nothing.

00:07:12.020 --> 00:07:14.640
You know, their warning was transmitted over every monitor on the base.

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:18.180
I've been to Central Computer.

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:20.850
Its memory cells have no record of any such planet.

00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:23.440
Of course, I haven't checked my own charts yet.

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:25.560
But if only we could speak to them.

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:28.390
Paul, any contact?

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:29.540
No response, sir.

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:32.820
They must be receiving.

00:07:35.060 --> 00:07:37.640
Ted Clifford wasn't transmitting classified information for nothing.

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:42.840
Well, if they won't talk to us, we'll just have to pay them a visit.

00:07:43.510 --> 00:07:45.210
I don't think it'll be a surprise.

00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:48.540
I've got a nasty feeling we're being watched.

00:08:17.310 --> 00:08:21.890
We've actually seen it, Commander, at the base of the brain and the cerebellum.

00:08:21.890 --> 00:08:30.000
Yes, a ball of orange light, very weak, pulsating, and then it died out. There was very little

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:40.280
left to examine. Most of it had melted. Melted? The analysis shows that the cerebrum, which

00:08:40.280 --> 00:08:45.330
regulates speech, hearing, and most important in this case, vision, had expanded to three

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:50.660
times its normal size. The neuronal system, which transmits information to the body through

00:08:50.660 --> 00:08:56.080
the nerves, was functioning at perhaps a thousand times its normal speed. Together,

00:08:56.220 --> 00:08:59.580
they somehow enabled Ted Clifford to see and act.

00:09:00.280 --> 00:09:01.280
As though he were a computer.

00:09:02.760 --> 00:09:11.490
Alan, a thorough survey.

00:09:11.950 --> 00:09:12.770
2-0 altitude.

00:09:13.580 --> 00:09:14.580
See if a landing's possible.

00:09:15.300 --> 00:09:18.600
You can get closer if you can, but under no circumstances are you to touch down.

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:23.020
Well, these Tritoniums, they might not appreciate our looking them over, Commander.

00:09:23.530 --> 00:09:25.840
I don't think we should wait for them to make the next move.

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:27.270
We're taking a look.

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:28.150
That's the next move.

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:30.000
Yeah, well, it's the wrong one, Commander.

00:09:30.860 --> 00:09:32.100
They've already killed Ted Clifford.

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:34.410
Those are your orders, Carter.

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:36.180
Is that clear?

00:09:39.410 --> 00:09:40.390
Perfectly clear, Commander.

00:09:50.770 --> 00:09:52.330
Eagle 3 to main mission ready to lift off.

00:10:04.350 --> 00:10:05.150
Eagle 3 to Alpha.

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:08.430
All systems are A-OK.

00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:11.300
Range 105 and closing.

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:25.160
I can see a kind of a surface.

00:10:26.840 --> 00:10:29.450
Still closing.

00:10:35.050 --> 00:10:39.090
Commander, there's a beam of light being projected from the sphere.

00:10:39.090 --> 00:10:40.800
Sir, scanner confirms.

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:51.510
I'm going for a 90 degree turn.

00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:02.700
It's no go, Commander.

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:06.050
Can't get away from the line.

00:11:06.050 --> 00:11:06.850
What's their range?

00:11:06.850 --> 00:11:07.750
3-5.

00:11:07.750 --> 00:11:09.000
Commander.

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:12.100
I can't hear you, Commander.

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:14.100
Range 2-0 and holding.

00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:15.600
Switch to automatic, Alan.

00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:20.140
The glare is increasing.

00:11:20.140 --> 00:11:21.340
You're heading into a first field.

00:11:21.340 --> 00:11:21.900
Wait a minute.

00:11:21.900 --> 00:11:23.240
Visibility zero.

00:11:34.640 --> 00:11:35.020
Answer me.

00:11:35.700 --> 00:11:36.540
It's no use, sir.

00:11:36.690 --> 00:11:49.210
Collision course.

00:11:50.530 --> 00:11:51.090
They're a manual.

00:11:53.050 --> 00:11:53.870
I can't bring them in.

00:11:56.660 --> 00:12:00.000
Should land close by, about 700 meters.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:04.030
Rescue and medical unit, stand by.

00:12:04.030 --> 00:12:06.580
Sir, there's no way to get to him.

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:09.650
We'll walk.

00:12:09.650 --> 00:12:18.950
They're down.

00:12:55.340 --> 00:12:57.460
and is dead, Commander. Carter is still alive.

00:12:57.770 --> 00:13:00.000
Paul, malfunction and scan assistance.

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:03.960
They've all gone dead.

00:13:03.960 --> 00:13:06.340
It's no accident, Paul.

00:13:06.340 --> 00:13:11.660
An attack.

00:13:11.660 --> 00:13:12.850
Commander?

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:13.770
Yes, Paul?

00:13:13.770 --> 00:13:15.480
We've jammed the scanner systems.

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:17.330
They're up to something.

00:13:17.330 --> 00:13:19.580
Might be a missile attack.

00:13:19.580 --> 00:13:21.640
We're more than halfway there.

00:13:21.640 --> 00:13:22.680
Go on to Carter's ship.

00:13:22.680 --> 00:13:25.620
I don't want to risk getting caught in the open.

00:13:25.620 --> 00:13:26.690
All right, let's go.

00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:24.640
- John? - It's all right.

00:15:24.640 --> 00:15:26.660
Easy, Commander, you'll be okay.

00:15:32.520 --> 00:15:34.560
- John.

00:15:34.560 --> 00:15:56.800
- Ah, they've taken Helena.

00:15:56.800 --> 00:15:58.200
All systems are working now.

00:16:00.220 --> 00:16:01.360
Through their force field somehow.

00:16:01.540 --> 00:16:03.160
What, without doing their energy source?

00:16:04.220 --> 00:16:08.710
What if we modify one of our eagles?

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:12.420
Double the power of our anti-gravity shields?

00:16:13.080 --> 00:16:14.380
Triple it, whatever the hell it takes.

00:16:14.480 --> 00:16:15.420
I don't know, it might work.

00:16:15.560 --> 00:16:16.700
I couldn't give you any guarantees.

00:16:16.960 --> 00:16:17.680
Work on it, Victor.

00:16:17.880 --> 00:16:18.180
All right.

00:16:19.400 --> 00:16:22.350
What about Carter?

00:16:22.760 --> 00:16:23.400
He'll make it.

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:24.240
Good.

00:16:25.430 --> 00:16:26.330
The co-pilot, Donovan?

00:16:26.810 --> 00:16:27.220
Dead.

00:16:28.290 --> 00:16:29.730
Now, they planned it, John.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:32.560
They just wanted to get Eleanor out there alone.

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:38.130
No, I don't think so.

00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:40.460
Why take Clifford?

00:16:40.950 --> 00:16:42.440
There's no connection.

00:16:43.490 --> 00:16:45.290
Maybe Dr. Russell is a hostage.

00:16:47.860 --> 00:16:48.440
For what reason?

00:16:50.670 --> 00:16:53.010
The way they killed Clifford?

00:16:54.230 --> 00:16:54.910
The shockwave?

00:16:56.010 --> 00:16:56.830
Locking us in orbit?

00:16:59.050 --> 00:16:59.390
No.

00:17:01.240 --> 00:17:02.740
they want from us in return

00:17:02.740 --> 00:17:05.800
they could simply

00:17:05.800 --> 00:17:08.920
just come and get it

00:17:08.920 --> 00:17:24.280
who are you? I am from the planet Earth

00:17:30.730 --> 00:17:33.210
- Then you know we mean you no harm.

00:17:33.210 --> 00:17:34.290
We need your help.

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:42.560
your instruments did they indicate anything no not a thing there's the light kept getting brighter

00:18:42.560 --> 00:18:51.350
sounds crazy a force field made of light that's exactly what it was lucky for me

00:18:51.350 --> 00:18:58.870
mara brought us in mara you'd switched out a manual

00:19:01.400 --> 00:19:02.500
You didn't land your ship for you.

00:19:02.760 --> 00:19:03.520
You were at the controls.

00:19:04.750 --> 00:19:05.010
Me?

00:19:06.190 --> 00:19:08.070
Oh, no, I was in Never Never Land.

00:19:11.420 --> 00:19:12.200
Get somewhere to tell him.

00:19:12.940 --> 00:19:13.540
Yeah, Commander.

00:19:17.070 --> 00:19:17.930
Where's Donovan?

00:19:42.410 --> 00:19:46.230
Look, John, the anti-gravity screen will neutralize the force field.

00:19:47.190 --> 00:19:50.060
It'll make a sort of corridor.

00:19:51.440 --> 00:19:53.440
It'll allow you to pass through and land.

00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:59.520
Merger.

00:20:03.770 --> 00:20:15.820
If we hit that light barrier, anything can happen.

00:20:15.820 --> 00:20:22.650
All set, Parks?

00:20:22.650 --> 00:20:25.430
I assigned Parks to this mission.

00:20:25.430 --> 00:20:27.670
Will we change places?

00:20:27.670 --> 00:20:29.410
Besides, Commander, I already know the way.

00:20:36.780 --> 00:20:37.730
- Have they gone?

00:20:37.730 --> 00:20:44.540
- Just lifting up now.

00:20:44.540 --> 00:20:49.490
- You know, anti-gravity shields, 50% power.

00:21:03.130 --> 00:21:05.010
Range 1-0-0.

00:21:09.620 --> 00:21:15.050
We're going to stay on manual, Paul.

00:21:31.760 --> 00:21:32.690
Scanner reading.

00:21:32.690 --> 00:21:33.780
You're clear, Commander.

00:21:33.780 --> 00:21:46.990
Gravity shield, full power.

00:21:46.990 --> 00:21:47.810
It's too soon, John.

00:21:47.810 --> 00:21:48.470
Full power.

00:22:08.060 --> 00:22:30.000
Velocity 7.5, range 5.0, range 3.5, velocity 8.3, velocity 8.5, V.

00:22:31.120 --> 00:22:32.660
8.7.

00:23:01.470 --> 00:23:02.910
9.1

00:23:02.910 --> 00:23:06.130
Victor, it's working

00:23:06.130 --> 00:23:09.120
We're getting through

00:23:30.570 --> 00:23:35.030
The engine! The engines!

00:24:00.410 --> 00:24:01.160
Alan!

00:24:35.020 --> 00:24:35.860
Sandra, anything?

00:24:36.250 --> 00:24:37.680
No visual or audio contact.

00:24:37.910 --> 00:24:42.450
How long now?

00:24:43.520 --> 00:24:44.260
A minute five.

00:24:47.150 --> 00:24:48.660
They are coming back.

00:24:52.970 --> 00:24:53.450
Any audio?

00:24:53.710 --> 00:24:54.150
No, sir.

00:24:54.370 --> 00:24:54.870
Commander Koenig.

00:24:55.530 --> 00:24:55.830
Commander.

00:24:56.410 --> 00:24:57.650
Have you still got them on automatic?

00:24:57.850 --> 00:24:58.110
Yes.

00:24:58.450 --> 00:24:59.130
Can you get them down?

00:24:59.460 --> 00:25:00.000
I'm switching.

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:05.280
in America, the remote control system.

00:25:05.280 --> 00:25:06.820
Eagle One on the main mission control.

00:25:38.890 --> 00:25:40.020
and do one touchdown.

00:26:09.180 --> 00:26:10.500
- What is it? - No idea.

00:26:39.530 --> 00:26:40.170
Really, I do.

00:26:42.390 --> 00:26:43.910
I'm sure you do.

00:26:48.340 --> 00:26:49.860
Why do doctors make the worst patients?

00:26:50.730 --> 00:26:52.660
Probably because we know too much.

00:26:53.750 --> 00:26:54.570
Blood pressure is normal.

00:26:54.930 --> 00:26:55.970
8 over 120.

00:26:56.530 --> 00:26:57.850
Bone marrow count, sugar.

00:26:58.850 --> 00:26:59.890
Everything checks out.

00:27:03.160 --> 00:27:03.620
You all right?

00:27:04.310 --> 00:27:06.580
I just felt faint for a moment.

00:27:08.140 --> 00:27:09.330
My equilibrium is off.

00:27:09.390 --> 00:27:11.010
Did you check my middle ear?

00:27:11.550 --> 00:27:12.390
Yes, it's perfect.

00:27:13.150 --> 00:27:13.840
Wait a minute.

00:27:35.760 --> 00:27:36.580
How many do you see?

00:27:37.310 --> 00:27:38.040
Two.

00:27:40.420 --> 00:27:46.290
I should see four.

00:27:49.520 --> 00:27:52.500
Did you check my optic hearing?

00:27:53.340 --> 00:27:55.590
Come on, Bob, tell me.

00:27:57.050 --> 00:27:58.170
Well, I can't explain it.

00:27:59.000 --> 00:28:00.000
But from all indications,

00:28:02.270 --> 00:28:02.970
You're blind.

00:28:06.120 --> 00:28:09.490
Well, obviously, she's not blind.

00:28:10.630 --> 00:28:10.990
Obviously.

00:28:13.750 --> 00:28:18.370
Do you have any explanation?

00:28:20.090 --> 00:28:20.750
Only one.

00:28:21.420 --> 00:28:22.040
Ted Clifford.

00:28:26.630 --> 00:28:28.690
Oh, another interesting account.

00:28:29.390 --> 00:28:29.940
And the pyramid.

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:38.270
texts of the old kingdom, but here they're called the eyes of heaven. Seems our friends

00:28:38.270 --> 00:28:44.420
get a bad a bit. I talked to them. I told them we meant them no harm and that we needed

00:28:44.420 --> 00:28:51.340
their help. You saw them? No, I only spoke to them, to a voice anyway. We know one thing

00:28:51.340 --> 00:28:57.750
about them. They can decompose atoms, reduce an object to its atomical components, cure

00:28:57.750 --> 00:29:00.000
energy, transport it through space.

00:29:00.160 --> 00:29:01.660
and reassemble it in another place.

00:29:01.920 --> 00:29:03.160
That's how they got you from here to there.

00:29:04.040 --> 00:29:06.440
Back on Earth, they've been working on that process for over 50 years.

00:29:06.810 --> 00:29:08.830
With machines, they do it with light.

00:29:09.280 --> 00:29:10.940
Yes, but what sort of light?

00:29:12.060 --> 00:29:12.740
And how?

00:29:13.450 --> 00:29:16.860
When I was in a sphere, I wasn't wearing my space suit.

00:29:18.960 --> 00:29:19.400
Oxygen.

00:29:22.070 --> 00:29:23.710
Tritonians might just be humanoid.

00:29:31.240 --> 00:29:44.790
John.

00:30:20.540 --> 00:30:22.370
- They've activated her like Clifford.

00:30:22.370 --> 00:30:23.850
She must be going to computer.

00:30:23.850 --> 00:30:26.570
- Notify Paul, no one's to try to stop her.

00:30:26.570 --> 00:30:28.160
- Paul, Bergman here.

00:30:36.750 --> 00:30:43.170
mission control to all sections alpha. Attention all personnel. Do not approach Dr. Russell.

00:30:43.920 --> 00:30:46.540
Repeat. Do not approach Dr. Russell.

00:31:13.500 --> 00:31:15.170
Don't touch her! Nobody touch her!

00:31:31.310 --> 00:31:34.020
What's the computer transmitting?

00:31:34.020 --> 00:31:43.380
SL371 Classified, the complete breakdown of our life support systems.

00:31:43.380 --> 00:31:45.650
Can't you stop it?

00:31:45.650 --> 00:31:48.770
Only if we stop her.

00:31:48.770 --> 00:31:52.160
The computer's not transmitting.

00:31:52.160 --> 00:31:53.560
Helena is.

00:32:29.470 --> 00:32:30.000
it is.

00:32:30.060 --> 00:32:33.240
She has 132 hours.

00:32:33.420 --> 00:32:35.060
That's five and a half days.

00:32:36.910 --> 00:32:37.890
That gives us some time.

00:32:39.900 --> 00:32:40.940
They exhaust the memory cells.

00:32:41.320 --> 00:32:41.800
What then?

00:32:43.410 --> 00:32:44.450
They won't need any of us.

00:32:44.880 --> 00:32:46.460
They won't need any of us now.

00:32:47.320 --> 00:32:48.880
Why don't they just come and get it over with?

00:32:50.790 --> 00:32:53.400
Perhaps they can't leave their sphere.

00:32:55.920 --> 00:32:57.760
That's it.

00:33:00.160 --> 00:33:01.160
Something's preventing them.

00:33:01.650 --> 00:33:02.770
They're limited in some way.

00:33:03.630 --> 00:33:04.070
Weakness.

00:33:05.040 --> 00:33:08.200
Everything they've done has only shown their advanced intelligence.

00:33:09.500 --> 00:33:10.740
No one's actually seen them.

00:33:10.920 --> 00:33:11.700
I mean, not even Helena.

00:33:12.320 --> 00:33:14.040
No, but we've been thinking of them as people.

00:33:14.800 --> 00:33:15.440
What if they're not?

00:33:16.400 --> 00:33:18.980
What if they're simply an intelligence with no physical form?

00:33:19.480 --> 00:33:20.780
They're just as trapped as we are.

00:33:21.270 --> 00:33:24.320
No, more so.

00:33:25.870 --> 00:33:26.650
We can still move.

00:33:26.750 --> 00:33:27.590
We can still get to them.

00:33:27.870 --> 00:33:30.000
Can't blast our way through their force field.

00:33:30.760 --> 00:33:39.030
but maybe we can bend it a little there it is commander ball of light just like ted clifford

00:33:39.030 --> 00:33:46.130
except it's stronger more alive the same with her cerebrum and her optic nerve now once dr

00:33:46.130 --> 00:33:53.640
s is activated this ball of light enables her to see well like a high-speed camera they needed

00:33:53.640 --> 00:33:58.060
her there to implant it that's why it didn't work on clifford it's their link

00:34:02.970 --> 00:34:06.260
True Helena, they're connected to our computer.

00:34:07.840 --> 00:34:09.940
Human conductor.

00:34:11.640 --> 00:34:14.100
Amanda, she can't take much more.

00:34:23.400 --> 00:34:30.000
That's real.

00:34:31.980 --> 00:34:41.430
information. Our knowledge, that's all. They're a sort of reconnaissance team sent out into space

00:34:41.430 --> 00:34:48.430
to gather information and then transmit it back to Triton. That's all. We did it ourselves with our

00:34:48.430 --> 00:34:59.320
deep space probe ships. Then Triton does exist. Oh, did exist. Now, this position of this mythological planet...

00:35:00.480 --> 00:35:06.230
does correspond to our galaxy charts, and I've checked it myself a dozen times, even

00:35:06.230 --> 00:35:16.090
through computer. But Triton is dead, John. Blew up. Disintegrated.

00:35:16.090 --> 00:35:19.470
So it's possible whoever programmed Helena and killed Ted Clifford doesn't know their

00:35:19.470 --> 00:35:24.500
planet no longer exists. If I can convince them their mission is obsolete, they might

00:35:24.500 --> 00:35:30.000
release her. Unfortunately, we're running out of time. I mean,

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:33.700
Helena's been activated six times in the last 24 hours.

00:35:34.610 --> 00:35:36.970
She's not going to survive another five and a half days.

00:35:38.590 --> 00:35:41.590
Now, they've miscalculated on their weakest link.

00:35:42.260 --> 00:35:43.560
She's not their weakest link, Victor.

00:35:47.400 --> 00:36:00.000
The circuit runs from their computers to the force field, around us, to Helena, Cano,

00:36:00.380 --> 00:36:03.380
- And back to their computers.

00:36:03.380 --> 00:36:08.680
Right, so it's all up to Kano, to jam computer.

00:36:08.680 --> 00:36:15.450
We can't touch Helena, but we can break the chain.

00:36:15.450 --> 00:36:16.490
- You tested it?

00:36:16.490 --> 00:36:17.900
- Only once, but it worked.

00:36:17.900 --> 00:36:18.820
When I jammed computer,

00:36:18.820 --> 00:36:20.860
the force field was turned off for 3.2 seconds.

00:36:20.860 --> 00:36:26.260
- Listen, you won't even get off the ground.

00:36:26.260 --> 00:36:27.950
- I'll need at least 15 minutes.

00:36:27.950 --> 00:36:30.000
- 13 minutes, 10 seconds from lift off

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:34.840
getting through the force field which of course won't be there and you can get me the 13 minutes

00:36:34.840 --> 00:36:40.030
plus 10 seconds it's easy like jamming a typewriter three keys locked together is not the same as

00:36:40.030 --> 00:36:47.130
locking them all when connor was experimenting he only jammed one circuit now he set up enough

00:36:47.130 --> 00:36:53.580
memory cells to cause an overload in 25 key circuits it'll take computer 32 seconds to

00:36:53.580 --> 00:36:58.190
clear each of those circuits which will give us the time we need 13 minutes

00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:04.880
computer jams the force field shut down just long enough for me to get through with a few seconds

00:37:04.880 --> 00:37:11.090
for margin even if it works what can you do when you get there how will you get inside the sphere

00:37:11.090 --> 00:37:17.340
the same way you did helena i don't think they know their planet no longer exists

00:37:17.340 --> 00:37:24.060
if i can convince them of that they may release you but there's no time pattern i'm

00:37:24.060 --> 00:37:30.000
activated at random helena please victor and carno have

00:37:30.160 --> 00:37:54.930
out the details all we need now is for you to go through with it choice to it was reactivated

00:38:10.010 --> 00:38:10.980
- -

00:38:32.940 --> 00:38:35.250
Remanda, Dr. Russell's been reactivated.

00:38:35.250 --> 00:38:36.400
Lift off.

00:39:22.360 --> 00:39:29.440
force field 8-0, 7-0, 6-0,

00:39:31.500 --> 00:39:32.990
Hulsefield.

00:39:32.990 --> 00:39:35.560
Four-zero.

00:39:35.560 --> 00:39:36.590
Three-zero.

00:39:36.590 --> 00:39:38.200
Kano, how are we on time?

00:39:38.200 --> 00:39:39.600
Any moment now.

00:40:16.730 --> 00:40:19.530
- Visual contact lost.

00:40:19.530 --> 00:40:21.600
- Commander Koenig.

00:40:21.600 --> 00:40:22.120
- Commander.

00:40:48.460 --> 00:40:50.200
This is main mission coming, Commander Koenig.

00:41:09.850 --> 00:41:10.530
Eagle one here.

00:41:11.640 --> 00:41:13.400
We're inside the sphere.

00:41:13.940 --> 00:41:14.460
They're through.

00:41:16.400 --> 00:41:16.900
That trick.

00:41:22.120 --> 00:41:23.420
Reactivated in a few minutes.

00:41:24.950 --> 00:41:25.760
For the last time.

00:41:30.920 --> 00:41:37.520
information on triton is in place dr russell now you can only transmit what we want them to know

00:41:37.520 --> 00:41:45.440
all set all set sir right stand by well i was never one to turn down an invitation

00:41:45.440 --> 00:41:51.200
when was i no carter you stay with the ship if we're not back in 10 minutes 15 at the most

00:41:51.200 --> 00:41:59.620
you blast out of here right sir you won't need that

00:42:02.780 --> 00:42:03.240
All right.

00:42:43.820 --> 00:42:44.440
Get ready.

00:43:19.230 --> 00:43:19.750
Thank you.

00:43:30.640 --> 00:43:31.640
That's it.

00:43:31.640 --> 00:43:32.640
That's it.

00:43:32.640 --> 00:43:36.920
That's it.

00:43:36.920 --> 00:43:37.920
That's it.

00:43:37.920 --> 00:43:38.040
That's it.

00:44:17.630 --> 00:44:20.100
Why don't you show yourselves?

00:44:33.230 --> 00:44:40.150
surely i'm no threat to you you knew we would jam our computer

00:45:00.760 --> 00:45:01.730
Except you need me.

00:45:01.730 --> 00:45:03.590
Dr. Russell will not live long enough.

00:45:03.590 --> 00:45:04.450
I'm to replace her.

00:45:04.450 --> 00:45:07.880
The death is also necessary.

00:45:07.880 --> 00:45:11.590
We're of such primitive intelligence.

00:45:11.590 --> 00:45:12.590
Why do you seek our knowledge?

00:45:12.590 --> 00:45:17.930
For when we decide to invade our planet.

00:45:17.930 --> 00:45:19.930
Triton is two million light years away.

00:45:19.930 --> 00:45:22.640
It's an illusion.

00:45:22.640 --> 00:45:27.990
Not to us, and not to you.

00:45:27.990 --> 00:45:30.000
Because your planet no longer exists.

00:45:30.990 --> 00:45:31.890
I can prove it!

00:45:31.890 --> 00:45:33.740
Right, stand by.

00:45:33.740 --> 00:45:38.560
Do not wish to destroy your men, Commander.

00:45:38.560 --> 00:45:43.680
Necessary.

00:45:43.680 --> 00:45:47.990
It won't be necessary, because I can prove to you that Triton no longer exists!

00:45:47.990 --> 00:45:50.160
Victor!

00:45:50.160 --> 00:45:53.840
She's setting the computations now.

00:46:00.380 --> 00:46:01.420
This is Triton's galaxy.

00:46:02.370 --> 00:46:02.810
Do you acknowledge?

00:46:04.830 --> 00:46:10.170
This is Triton's star system.

00:46:13.580 --> 00:46:17.760
This is Triton's universe.

00:46:22.720 --> 00:46:27.040
This is Triton's sun.

00:46:33.040 --> 00:46:36.040
The calculations and confirmation you're receiving now are coming through Dr. Russell.

00:46:36.700 --> 00:46:37.340
You can check them.

00:46:39.640 --> 00:46:42.720
They will prove beyond a doubt that your sun exploded,

00:46:43.160 --> 00:46:46.340
that Triton and the other planets in your solar system have been destroyed.

00:46:46.800 --> 00:46:48.060
Triton no longer exists.

00:46:48.540 --> 00:46:49.860
Your function is discontinued.

00:46:50.020 --> 00:46:51.460
And release Dr. Russell and my men.

00:47:01.630 --> 00:47:02.910
Die. Die.

00:47:30.120 --> 00:47:32.090
- Let's get out of here, move it.

00:47:32.090 --> 00:47:41.550
- Right.

00:47:41.550 --> 00:47:45.790
- You are so good, your feet got out.

00:47:45.790 --> 00:47:47.930
- The instruments show the sphere is breaking up.

00:47:47.930 --> 00:47:51.590
- What about the force field?

00:47:51.590 --> 00:47:52.750
- It's lost its power.

00:47:52.750 --> 00:47:53.750
- Visual contact.

00:48:22.650 --> 00:48:24.450
to satisfy my curiosity.

00:48:31.820 --> 00:48:32.320
What is it?

00:48:32.620 --> 00:48:35.030
You have a lovely optic nerve, Dr. Russell.

00:48:35.960 --> 00:48:37.200
Thank you, Doctor.

00:48:43.350 --> 00:48:44.350
Why so pensive, Victor?

00:48:45.830 --> 00:48:50.250
Oh, I was just thinking about that planet, Triton.

00:48:52.250 --> 00:48:53.490
All that knowledge.

00:49:00.510 --> 00:49:02.790
Perhaps knowledge isn't the answer after all.

00:49:02.790 --> 00:49:07.680
What is?
